id: pm-vcs-jeun
title: "pm vcs items: map a commit range onto the pm items it touched"
description: Joins git history to the pm ledger so a PR description or release note can state which tracked work a branch represents.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:package",merge-safety
created_at: "2026-07-30T10:51:32.280Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T10:52:08.495Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-30T10:52:08.476Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-30T10:52:08.476Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: Items are classified created/modified/deleted with the earliest change deciding kind and a later deletion outranking it; history streams and settings are not double-counted; ordering is deterministic
parent: pm-vcs-ghql
resolution: Implemented and covered.
expected_result: The command behaves as its acceptance criteria describe.
actual_result: "59 tests pass; coverage is 100% lines, branches and functions across all five source files, stable across three consecutive gate runs."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T10:51:49.334Z","harness:claude-code","git log --name-status -z separates a record's formatted header from its first name-status entry with a NEWLINE, not a NUL. Without trimming the status token the first changed path of every commit carries status '\\nA', which fails a startsWith('A') test and silently reports a newly added item as modified — a wrong answer in the exact field a changelog reads, not an error. Caught by the created/modified/deleted test."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  ledger.ts,project,git-to-pm range join
  test/ledger.test.ts,project,8 tests over real commit ranges
close_reason: "Shipped in the initial release behind the 100/100/100 coverage gate, verified against real git repositories."
body: ""
